IMPORT prelude
IMPORT `art-dates`
IMPORT `art-applicant`

-- Administrative Review Tribunal Act 2024 (Cth) -- cases for the applicant's seat (art-applicant.l4).
-- Every expected value was worked by hand from the deposited text (C2026C00202), section by section, before the encoding
-- was run. Dates are counted with the day of the event excluded: "within 28 days after" 2 March is up to 30 March.
-- HYPOTHETICAL facts throughout. BASELINE ENCODING. Not for public use as advice.

GIVEN d IS A DEONTIC `Applicant party` `Review step`
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`ends fulfilled` d MEANS
    CONSIDER d
    WHEN FULFILLED THEN TRUE
    OTHERWISE FALSE

GIVEN d IS A NUMBER, m IS A NUMBER, y IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A DATE
`on` d m y MEANS `the calendar date` d m y

§ `Notice and reasons (Part 10)`

-- s 266. Ana's incapacity payments are cut by a Commonwealth decision she can take to the Tribunal: notice is owed.
#ASSERT `Must the decision-maker tell me of the decision and my review rights question` TRUE FALSE TRUE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE EQUALS JUST TRUE
-- A decision of the Tribunal itself, or of a court: s 266(2), the section does not reach it.
#ASSERT `Must the decision-maker tell me of the decision and my review rights question` TRUE TRUE TRUE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE EQUALS NOTHING
-- No reviewable decision in the pathway.
#ASSERT `Must the decision-maker tell me of the decision and my review rights question` FALSE FALSE TRUE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE EQUALS NOTHING
-- Her interests are not affected: s 266(4) is silent about her.
#ASSERT `Must the decision-maker tell me of the decision and my review rights question` TRUE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE EQUALS NOTHING
-- s 266(6)(a), (b): another law sets the notice; a refusal deemed under s 16.
#ASSERT `Must the decision-maker tell me of the decision and my review rights question` TRUE FALSE TRUE TRUE FALSE FALSE FALSE EQUALS JUST FALSE
#ASSERT `Must the decision-maker tell me of the decision and my review rights question` TRUE FALSE TRUE FALSE TRUE FALSE FALSE EQUALS JUST FALSE
-- s 266(6)(c): wholly favourable and harming no one: no notice owed; harming another person: notice owed again.
#ASSERT `Must the decision-maker tell me of the decision and my review rights question` TRUE FALSE TRUE FALSE FALSE TRUE FALSE EQUALS JUST FALSE
#ASSERT `Must the decision-maker tell me of the decision and my review rights question` TRUE FALSE TRUE FALSE FALSE TRUE TRUE EQUALS JUST TRUE

-- s 268 with s 12 and s 15.
#ASSERT `Can I ask for a statement of reasons question` TRUE FALSE TRUE FALSE FALSE FALSE EQUALS JUST TRUE
-- s 12(2): reviewable because decisions under the power are, though the maker was not authorised.
#ASSERT `Can I ask for a statement of reasons question` FALSE TRUE TRUE FALSE FALSE FALSE EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `Can I ask for a statement of reasons question` FALSE FALSE TRUE FALSE FALSE FALSE EQUALS NOTHING
-- Not affected: s 269(6) obliges refusal.
#ASSERT `Can I ask for a statement of reasons question` TRUE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE EQUALS JUST FALSE
-- s 15: an injured workers' association whose objects included the matter when the decision was made.
#ASSERT `Can I ask for a statement of reasons question` TRUE FALSE FALSE TRUE TRUE FALSE EQUALS JUST TRUE
-- ... but it has since removed the matter from its objects (s 15(b)).
#ASSERT `Can I ask for a statement of reasons question` TRUE FALSE FALSE TRUE TRUE TRUE EQUALS JUST FALSE

-- s 269. The decision letter was given on 1 March 2026. A request on 29 March 2026 (day 28) is in time; on 30 March (day 29)
-- the decision-maker may refuse it as late (s 269(8)(a)).
#ASSERT `What happens to my request for reasons question` TRUE TRUE FALSE TRUE (`on` 1 3 2026) (`on` 29 3 2026) FALSE FALSE FALSE EQUALS `the decision-maker must give me a statement of reasons within 28 days after receiving my request (s 269(2)), and tell me of anything removed (s 269(3)-(5))`
#ASSERT `What happens to my request for reasons question` TRUE TRUE FALSE TRUE (`on` 1 3 2026) (`on` 30 3 2026) FALSE FALSE FALSE EQUALS `the decision-maker may refuse: my request was late (s 269(8)); a refusal needs written notice within 28 days (s 269(11), (12))`
-- No decision document: lateness is the decision-maker's "reasonable time" (s 269(8)(b)), an input.
#ASSERT `What happens to my request for reasons question` TRUE TRUE FALSE FALSE (`on` 1 3 2026) (`on` 30 9 2026) TRUE FALSE FALSE EQUALS `the decision-maker may refuse: my request was late (s 269(8)); a refusal needs written notice within 28 days (s 269(11), (12))`
#ASSERT `What happens to my request for reasons question` TRUE TRUE FALSE FALSE (`on` 1 3 2026) (`on` 30 9 2026) FALSE FALSE FALSE EQUALS `the decision-maker must give me a statement of reasons within 28 days after receiving my request (s 269(2)), and tell me of anything removed (s 269(3)-(5))`
#ASSERT `What happens to my request for reasons question` FALSE TRUE FALSE TRUE (`on` 1 3 2026) (`on` 2 3 2026) FALSE FALSE FALSE EQUALS `not covered: the decision is not reviewable, so Part 10 Division 3 does not apply`
#ASSERT `What happens to my request for reasons question` TRUE FALSE FALSE TRUE (`on` 1 3 2026) (`on` 2 3 2026) FALSE FALSE FALSE EQUALS `the decision-maker must refuse: my interests are not affected (s 269(6)); written notice of refusal within 28 days (s 269(11), (12))`
-- Already given reasons, and also late: s 269(7) is answered first (no refusal notice needed).
#ASSERT `What happens to my request for reasons question` TRUE TRUE TRUE TRUE (`on` 1 3 2026) (`on` 30 3 2026) FALSE FALSE FALSE EQUALS `the decision-maker may refuse: I have already been given a statement of reasons (s 269(7)); no refusal notice is needed`
#ASSERT `What happens to my request for reasons question` TRUE TRUE FALSE TRUE (`on` 1 3 2026) (`on` 2 3 2026) FALSE TRUE FALSE EQUALS `the decision-maker may refuse: the reasons would disclose information about another person that cannot practicably be removed (s 269(9)); written notice within 28 days`
#ASSERT `What happens to my request for reasons question` TRUE TRUE FALSE TRUE (`on` 1 3 2026) (`on` 2 3 2026) FALSE FALSE TRUE EQUALS `the decision-maker may refuse: a public interest certificate covers information the statement cannot leave out without misleading (s 269(10)); written notice within 28 days`

-- s 269(2), (12)(b): request received 2 March 2026; answer due by 30 March 2026.
#ASSERT `By when must the decision-maker answer my request for reasons question` (`on` 2 3 2026) EQUALS `on` 30 3 2026

-- The s 269 rule: an answer on day 28 fulfils it; on day 29 it does not.
#ASSERT `ends fulfilled` (EVALTRACE `s 269 -- the decision-maker must answer my request for reasons within 28 days` 0 (LIST (EVENT `the decision-maker` `answer my request for reasons (a statement of reasons or a written refusal)` 28)))
#ASSERT `ends fulfilled` (EVALTRACE `s 269 -- the decision-maker must answer my request for reasons within 28 days` 0 (LIST (EVENT `the decision-maker` `answer my request for reasons (a statement of reasons or a written refusal)` 0)))
#ASSERT (NOT (`ends fulfilled` (EVALTRACE `s 269 -- the decision-maker must answer my request for reasons within 28 days` 0 (LIST (WAITUNTIL 29), (EVENT `the decision-maker` `answer my request for reasons (a statement of reasons or a written refusal)` 29)))))
-- expect: BREACH by the decision-maker (no answer within 28 days; s 270(1)(b))
#TRACE `s 269 -- the decision-maker must answer my request for reasons within 28 days` AT 0 WITH
    (WAITUNTIL 29)
    PARTY `the decision-maker` DOES `answer my request for reasons (a statement of reasons or a written refusal)` AT 29

