-- s 16: a 90-day period to determine a claim ended on 30 April 2026 with no determination: a refusal is deemed that day.
#ASSERT `Is a refusal taken to have been made because time ran out question` TRUE TRUE (`on` 30 4 2026) FALSE EQUALS JUST (`on` 30 4 2026)
#ASSERT `Is a refusal taken to have been made because time ran out question` TRUE TRUE (`on` 30 4 2026) TRUE EQUALS NOTHING
#ASSERT `Is a refusal taken to have been made because time ran out question` TRUE FALSE (`on` 30 4 2026) FALSE EQUALS NOTHING
#ASSERT `Is a refusal taken to have been made because time ran out question` FALSE TRUE (`on` 30 4 2026) FALSE EQUALS NOTHING

-- s 18(3): decision made 3 February 2026 (February 2026 has 28 days): the rules' period cannot end before 3 March 2026.
#ASSERT `What is the earliest my time to apply can end question` (`on` 3 2 2026) EQUALS `on` 3 3 2026
#ASSERT `What is the earliest my time to apply can end question` (`on` 1 4 2026) EQUALS `on` 29 4 2026

-- s 18 in time. The rules give 28 days from the decision of 1 April 2026: the last day is 29 April 2026.
#ASSERT `Am I in time to apply question` `the Tribunal's rules (s 18(1))` (`on` 1 4 2026) (`on` 1 4 2026) 28 TRUE (`on` 29 4 2026) (`on` 1 5 2026) FALSE (`on` 1 1 2026) EQUALS `yes: within the prescribed period (s 18(1))`
#ASSERT `Am I in time to apply question` `the Tribunal's rules (s 18(1))` (`on` 1 4 2026) (`on` 1 4 2026) 28 TRUE (`on` 30 4 2026) (`on` 1 5 2026) FALSE (`on` 1 1 2026) EQUALS `out of time: I need the Tribunal to extend the period (s 19); it may do so even after the period has expired`
#ASSERT `Am I in time to apply question` `the Tribunal's rules (s 18(1))` (`on` 1 4 2026) (`on` 1 4 2026) 28 FALSE (`on` 1 1 2026) (`on` 29 4 2026) FALSE (`on` 1 1 2026) EQUALS `not yet late: the period has not ended`
#ASSERT `Am I in time to apply question` `the Tribunal's rules (s 18(1))` (`on` 1 4 2026) (`on` 1 4 2026) 28 FALSE (`on` 1 1 2026) (`on` 30 4 2026) FALSE (`on` 1 1 2026) EQUALS `out of time: I need the Tribunal to extend the period (s 19); it may do so even after the period has expired`
-- Applying on the day of the decision itself.
#ASSERT `Am I in time to apply question` `the Tribunal's rules (s 18(1))` (`on` 1 4 2026) (`on` 1 4 2026) 28 TRUE (`on` 1 4 2026) (`on` 1 5 2026) FALSE (`on` 1 1 2026) EQUALS `yes: within the prescribed period (s 18(1))`
-- Extended to 15 May 2026: an application on 15 May is within it; on 16 May it is not.
#ASSERT `Am I in time to apply question` `the Tribunal's rules (s 18(1))` (`on` 1 4 2026) (`on` 1 4 2026) 28 TRUE (`on` 15 5 2026) (`on` 20 5 2026) TRUE (`on` 15 5 2026) EQUALS `the Tribunal has extended the period (s 19), and I am within it`
#ASSERT `Am I in time to apply question` `the Tribunal's rules (s 18(1))` (`on` 1 4 2026) (`on` 1 4 2026) 28 TRUE (`on` 16 5 2026) (`on` 20 5 2026) TRUE (`on` 15 5 2026) EQUALS `out of time: I need the Tribunal to extend the period (s 19); it may do so even after the period has expired`
-- A rules period entered as 21 days from the decision would end on 22 April, before the s 18(3) floor of 29 April.
#ASSERT `Am I in time to apply question` `the Tribunal's rules (s 18(1))` (`on` 1 4 2026) (`on` 1 4 2026) 21 TRUE (`on` 10 4 2026) (`on` 10 4 2026) FALSE (`on` 1 1 2026) EQUALS `not covered: the rules' period as entered ends before the earliest end the rules may set (s 18(3))`
-- The same 21 days set by the Act the decision was made under is not bound by s 18(3): 22 April is the last day.
#ASSERT `Am I in time to apply question` `the Act or instrument the decision was made under` (`on` 1 4 2026) (`on` 1 4 2026) 21 TRUE (`on` 22 4 2026) (`on` 22 4 2026) FALSE (`on` 1 1 2026) EQUALS `yes: within the prescribed period (s 18(1))`
#ASSERT `Am I in time to apply question` `the Act or instrument the decision was made under` (`on` 1 4 2026) (`on` 1 4 2026) 21 TRUE (`on` 23 4 2026) (`on` 23 4 2026) FALSE (`on` 1 1 2026) EQUALS `out of time: I need the Tribunal to extend the period (s 19); it may do so even after the period has expired`
-- The rules' period counted from the day the decision was given to me (8 April 2026), 28 days: last day 6 May 2026.
#ASSERT `Am I in time to apply question` `the Tribunal's rules (s 18(1))` (`on` 1 4 2026) (`on` 8 4 2026) 28 TRUE (`on` 6 5 2026) (`on` 6 5 2026) FALSE (`on` 1 1 2026) EQUALS `yes: within the prescribed period (s 18(1))`
#ASSERT `Am I in time to apply question` `no law sets a period` (`on` 1 4 2026) (`on` 1 4 2026) 0 TRUE (`on` 1 4 2027) (`on` 1 4 2027) FALSE (`on` 1 1 2026) EQUALS `no period applies: in time unless the Tribunal considers I did not apply within a reasonable time (s 20)`

-- The s 18 rule itself.
#ASSERT `ends fulfilled` (EVALTRACE (`s 18 -- I must apply within the prescribed period` 28) 0 (LIST (EVENT `I, the applicant` `apply to the Tribunal for review` 28)))
#ASSERT (NOT (`ends fulfilled` (EVALTRACE (`s 18 -- I must apply within the prescribed period` 28) 0 (LIST (WAITUNTIL 29), (EVENT `I, the applicant` `apply to the Tribunal for review` 29)))))
-- expect: BREACH by the applicant (no application within the prescribed period; s 19 extension is the route)
#TRACE `s 18 -- I must apply within the prescribed period` 28 AT 0 WITH
